  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DetailsOfTheEntityHaveProcessesInPlaceToAvoidOrManageConflictOfInterestsInvolvingMembersOfTheBoardExplanatoryTextBlock' (DetailsOfTheEntityHaveProcessesInPlaceToAvoidOrManageConflictOfInterestsInvolvingMembersOfTheBoardExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Yes. Kindly refer to the section titled “Material aspects of Corporate Governance and TCS’ approach to them” in the Corporate Governance Report, which forms part of this Integrated Annual Report.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DetailsOfTheEntityHaveProcessesInPlaceToAvoidOrManageConflictOfInterestsInvolvingMembersOfTheBoardExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'NotesPrinciple1ExplanatoryTextBlock' (NotesPrinciple1ExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'The United States Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit, Northern District of Texas upheld an award of US$56 million in compensatory damages and US$112 million in exemplary damages apart from prejudgment interest of US$26 million, in favour of Computer Sciences Corporation (CSC)/ DXC Technology Company (DXC) against the Company, in connection with alleged misappropriation of its trade secrets. The Company has filed a writ of certiorari in the Supreme Court of the United States and intends to vigorously defend its position.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: NotesPrinciple1ExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'TotalNumberOfAwarenessProgrammesHeld' (TotalNumberOfAwarenessProgrammesHeld) is '3184' xbrli:pure.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: TotalNumberOfAwarenessProgrammesHeld, Context: D_AwarenessProgrammesConductedForValueChainPartners1)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'TopicsOrPrinciplesCoveredUnderTheTraining' (TopicsOrPrinciplesCoveredUnderTheTraining) is 'Principle 3: Awareness on safe work at height, use of personal protective equipment, first-aid and medical emergency, incident reporting, housekeeping awareness, slip, trip, falls, health awareness, electrical safety, ergonomics and manual material handling, chemical safety, food safety, noise and\nindoor air quality monitoring, HSE legal requirement, lock-out and tag-out, permit to work, road safety, etc.\nPrinciple 6: Environmental Awareness – Overview- noise pollution, energy conservation, waste disposal and air pollution.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: TopicsOrPrinciplesCoveredUnderTheTraining, Context: D_AwarenessProgrammesConductedForValueChainPartners1)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'PercentageOfValueChainPartnersCoveredUnderTheAwarenessProgrammes' (PercentageOfValueChainPartnersCoveredUnderTheAwarenessProgrammes) is '1' xbrli:pure.",
