  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'NameOfTheArea' (NameOfTheArea) is 'In FY 2026, there are 25 stress zones* locations respectively identified as per the classification by the Central Ground Water Board for India locations and the World Resources Institute (WRI) Aqueduct Tool for non-India geographies. 55 TCS offices are located under water stressed zones. List of the 25 stress zones is as below: Ambattur (1 TCS location) , Bengaluru (North) (1 TCS location), Bisrakh (5 TCS locations), Gurugram (4 TCS locations), Karol Bagh (1 TCS location), Serilingampally (5 TCS locations), Varanasi (1 TCS location), Anekal (1 TCS location), Bengaluru (East) (8 TCS locations), Mambalam ( 1 TCS Location), Gandhinagar (2 TCS locations), Indore (1 TCS location),  Lucknow (1 TCS location), Vadodara (1 TCS location), Velachery (1 TCS Location), Japan (2 TCS locations), US (1 TCS locations), China (4 TCS Locations), Philippines (3 TCS locations), Israel (1 TCS location),  Chile (2 TCS locations), Mexico (5 TCS locations), Egmore (1 TCS Location), Uruguay (1 TCS location) and Saudi Arabia (1 TCS Location).\n*The data for water stressed locations across TCS global (including top 20 non -India locations which attributes to 50% of overseas water consumption) has been included in FY 2026. For TCS India operations the Central Ground Water Authority (CGWA), India and for other geographies the WRI Aqueduct have been used to identify water stressed locations respectively.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: NameOfTheArea, Context: D_FacilityOrPlantLocatedInAreasOfWaterStress1)"
  },
